// Auto-generated from legacy HTML by scripts/extract-pages.py
export const title = "Genetec Integration Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Genetec Integration Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.1 Prerequisites</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>AIBridge FW version 1035xx or greater.</li>\n<li>Genetec Security Center 5.11 or greater.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.2 Understanding the Integration Architecture</h3>\n<p>There are two ways to integrate AIBridge with Genetec VMS.</p>\n\n<p><strong>1) Case 1</strong></p>\n<p>AIBridge receives the RTSP video stream from the IP camera, performs AI analysis, and provides an annotated video stream along with event data. The video is transcoded to include object recognition data, bounding boxes, and zone information.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 260\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"135\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <rect x=\"600\" y=\"30\" width=\"150\" height=\"90\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f2f3f6\" stroke=\"#9aa0ac\"/>\n  <text x=\"675\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\" font-weight=\"700\">Genetec</text>\n  <rect x=\"600\" y=\"170\" width=\"130\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#0b0f19\"/>\n  <text x=\"665\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\">AI Bridge</text>\n  <line x1=\"335\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"590\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#arrn)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"675\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"665\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#e0a94c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrn)\" marker-start=\"url(#arrn)\"/>\n  <text x=\"700\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#7a4f10\">AI Event &amp;<tspan x=\"700\" dy=\"14\">Annotated Video</tspan></text>\n  <line x1=\"335\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"590\" y2=\"215\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#arrn)\"/>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrn\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f9c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Case 1 &mdash; AIBridge receives RTSP from IP cameras and sends AI events &amp; annotated video to Genetec</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong>2) Case 2</strong></p>\n<p>Both AIBridge and Genetec VMS receive the RTSP stream from the IP camera at the same time, and AIBridge sends only the AI analysis events directly to Genetec VMS. Instead of receiving the RTSP stream directly from the IP camera, AIBridge can also pull the RTSP stream from Genetec VMS.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 260\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <rect x=\"330\" y=\"20\" width=\"170\" height=\"80\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f2f3f6\" stroke=\"#9aa0ac\"/>\n  <text x=\"415\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\" font-weight=\"700\">Genetec VMS</text>\n  <rect x=\"360\" y=\"190\" width=\"130\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#0b0f19\"/>\n  <text x=\"425\" y=\"225\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\">AI Bridge</text>\n  <line x1=\"415\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#e0a94c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrn2)\" marker-start=\"url(#arrn2)\"/>\n  <text x=\"440\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#7a4f10\">AI Event</text>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrn2\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#e0a94c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Case 2 &mdash; both systems receive RTSP directly; AIBridge sends only AI events to Genetec</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<h2>2. Configuration</h2>\n<p>Integrating events between AI Bridge and Genetec requires WebSDK registration, Genetec event configuration, and AI Bridge configuration. Each is explained below.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.1 WebSDK Setup</h3>\n<p>Confirm your license supports the WebSDK feature &ndash; without it, the integration won't work. A WebSDK license must be purchased to integrate AIBridge with Genetec.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\"><strong>Note.</strong> You'll need to request the license from Genetec (e.g. <code>GSC-1SDK-?????-??????</code>).</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>Go to <strong>Config Tool &rsaquo; Task &rsaquo; System &rsaquo; General settings</strong>. On the Roles tab, click <strong>Add an entity</strong> at the bottom left and add a <strong>Web SDK</strong> role.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:520px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:100px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Role Type</span><select disabled><option>Web-based SDK</option></select>\n    <span>Port</span><input value=\"4590\" disabled>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Process: Next &rarr; Create &rarr; Close. Enter the port number you want to use.</figcaption>\n</div>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#128712; TIP. If events aren't working correctly, check your firewall.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.2 Genetec Configuration</h3>\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:20px;font-size:16px;\">2.2.1 Adding a Device</h4>\n<p>To use annotated video, register AIBridge as a device. To use the original camera video, register the camera instead. For annotated video (Case 1), follow 2.2.1.1 below; for original video (Case 2), follow 2.2.1.2.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:20px;font-size:16px;\">2.2.1.1 Using Annotated Video (Case 1)</h4>\n<p>In Config Tool's Video section, add AI Bridge as a camera/device entity.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:20px;font-size:16px;\">2.2.1.2 Using Original Video (Case 2)</h4>\n<p>In Config Tool's Video section, add the camera directly.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:20px;font-size:16px;\">2.2.2 Event and Action Settings</h4>\n<p>Once the device is registered, follow these steps in Genetec to register the AI event:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Config Tool &rsaquo; Task &rsaquo; System &rsaquo; General settings</strong>.</li>\n<li>In the Events panel, click the <strong>+</strong> button at the bottom left to add an AI event.</li>\n<li>In the <strong>When</strong> selector, choose the AI event you just created. On the Actions tab, choose the action and camera you want (this guide uses a bookmark).</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#8251; The Actions tab supports several different output events, shown in the figure below &ndash; use whichever fits your needs.</p>\n</div>\n<p>To use a different alarm per AIBridge channel, assign a video channel to each one and create the alarms sequentially, following the same pattern shown in the example.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:20px;font-size:16px;\">2.2.3 Alarm Monitoring Event Setup</h4>\n<p>Go to the Alarm tab in Config Tool and configure it as follows (you're free to choose any camera). For the AI event created earlier, select <strong>Trigger Alarm</strong>, and for Alarm, choose the alarm you created above.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.3 AIBridge Configuration</h3>\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:20px;font-size:16px;\">2.3.1 Adding a Camera</h4>\n<p>A camera must be registered to use AI video analysis. In AIBridge's left menu, go to the <strong>Video Stream</strong> tab and click <strong>Search Cameras</strong>. Set the search method to <strong>Onvif</strong> and click <strong>Search Cameras</strong>.</p>\n<p>Find the camera to register in the list and enter its ID and password, then choose the channel to assign the stream to and click <strong>Submit</strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>Camera</th><th>Channel</th><th>Status</th></tr>\n<tr><td>192.168.101.21</td><td>CH 1</td><td style=\"color:var(--green);\">&#9679; Registered</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Once registration finishes, the camera appears in the list like this</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:20px;font-size:16px;\">2.3.2 Adding an AI App</h4>\n<p>This section creates the AIBridge event. In the left menu, go to <strong>App Settings &rsaquo; Explore AI Apps</strong>, and select the AI feature you want from the available options.</p>\n<p>AIBridge ships with 50+ AI apps ready to use &ndash; see the full app catalog for details. This example uses Intrusion Detection.</p>\n<p>Click <strong>Add Rule</strong>, add the event setting, configure the zone, then click <strong>Apply</strong>.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:20px;font-size:16px;\">2.3.3 Action Handler Setup</h4>\n<p>Add an action setting, choose <strong>Genetec</strong> as the action type, and check the box. Edit the Genetec server settings:</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:460px;\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\">\n  <div class=\"modal-head\">Genetec Server</div>\n  <div class=\"modal-body\">\n    <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:120px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n      <span>Host</span><input value=\"192.168.101.15\" disabled>\n      <span>Port</span><input value=\"4590\" disabled>\n      <span>Base URI</span><select disabled><option>WebSdk</option></select>\n      <span>Username</span><input disabled>\n      <span>Password</span><input disabled>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"modal-foot\"><span class=\"btn small\">Cancel</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Next</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Set the Genetec server host and the port number configured earlier, set the base URI to WebSdk, and enter the Genetec username and password</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p>For channel mapping, click <strong>Next</strong> and enter the Logical ID of the matching Genetec VMS camera for each AIBridge video channel. The Logical ID for each channel can be found on the Logical ID screen in Config Tool.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>AIBridge Channel</th><th>Genetec Logical ID</th></tr>\n<tr><td>CH 1</td><td><input value=\"101\" disabled style=\"width:80px;\"></td></tr>\n<tr><td>CH 2</td><td><input value=\"102\" disabled style=\"width:80px;\"></td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<p>You'll also need to enter the Custom Event Value created in section 2.2.2, which can be found under <strong>System &rsaquo; Events</strong> in Genetec Config Tool. Selecting <strong>Add Channel Number</strong> automatically appends the channel number to the Custom Event Value (e.g. Channel 1: 1001, Channel 2: 1002, Channel 8: 1008).</p>\n\n<p>To automatically create bookmarks, select <strong>Use Bookmark</strong>. Bookmarks can record information such as LPR data or object attributes, which you can view and search from the Bookmark menu in Genetec Security Desk.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#8251; For license plate recognition, Basic Notification + LPR is a convenient combination.</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>Once everything is configured, use the Test button to confirm the event integration is working. When an event is sent successfully, an alarm appears in Alarm Monitoring.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#128712; TIP. If events aren't working correctly, check your firewall.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>3. Demo</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.1 Live</h3>\n<p>Live video can be viewed from the Video tab in Config Tool.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.2 Bookmarks</h3>\n<p>Go to <strong>Genetec Security Desk &rsaquo; Task &rsaquo; Bookmarks</strong>, select the camera you want, then click the Report button.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#8251; Events don't update in real time, so click Report to refresh the list.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Check the bookmarks and video associated with the event that occurred.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.3 Alarm Monitoring</h3>\n<p>Alarms can be monitored in real time. In Security Desk, select the <strong>Alarm Monitoring</strong> menu to see live alarm monitoring information for the real-time alarm trigger event configured in section 2.2.3.</p>\n<p>As live events occur, you can review the alarm event and its related video channel while managing the alarm.</p>\n\n<h2>4. Revision History</h2>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>v1.00 &ndash; Initial document.</li>\n<li>v1.10 &ndash; Updated Section 2.3 with AI Bridge configuration details.</li>\n<li>v1.20 &ndash; Fixed document typos.</li>\n</ul>";
